---
title: Measurements
sidebar:
  label: Overview
  order: 0
---

The catalog format selected in `Settings` decides which measurement form a specimen shows. Each taxon group has its own page:

| Catalog format | Taxon group | Measurement page |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Mammalogy | Mammals | [Mammals](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/mammals/) |
| Ornithology | Birds | [Birds](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/birds/) |
| Herpetology (beta) | Herpetofauna | [Herpetofauna](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/herpetofauna/) |
| Invertebrate zoology (beta) | Invertebrates | [Invertebrates](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/invertebrates/) |
| Ichthyology (beta) | Fishes | [Fishes](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/fishes/) |
| Paleontology (in development) | Fossils | [Paleontology](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/paleontology/) |

Mammal catalogs can also show bat fields; see
[Mammals](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/mammals/#bat-fields).

Weight fields support `g`, `kg`, and `lbs` and default to `g`. Changing the
unit only changes the label; it does not convert the entered number.

Sex is a restricted controlled vocabulary shared by every taxon group. `Male`,
`Female`, and `Unknown` are always available. In `Settings` > `Specimens`, add
`Gynandromorph`, `Hermaphrodite`, `Female?`, or `Male?` to the dropdown. The
question mark records that the examiner is uncertain.

`Life stage` is also shared by every taxon group, and replaced the older
numeric age fields. It is an editable controlled vocabulary: the defaults are
`Egg`, `Larva`, `Nymph`, `Pupa`, `Neonate`, `Juvenile`, `Subadult`, `Adult`,
`Metamorph`, and `Unknown`, and the list is configured in `Settings` >
`Specimens` > `Life stages`.
